# A/B slider and group commands, sniffed from the original remotes, 2026-11-25
#
# Receiver: handheld PCB rev 1, board 1, with an nRF24 module, firmware
# v0.9.13, command `sniff` (ch 33, 2 Mbps, address E7E7E7, CRC-16, 5-byte
# payload). Channels 52 and 71 weren't sniffed.
#
# Remote IDs redacted: yy yy = working remote, xx xx = weak (damaged) remote.
# Lines are copied from the serial monitor; times at the left are the PC's.
# "# ..." lines inside a capture are the tester's (John's) notes.

## 1. Working remote, group 2, slider on A and then on B

# John's description: in each sequence, A and B, he started with the shades
# up, commanded them down, pressed the UP arrow to stop them, then pressed
# UP again to close. Both shades moved with the slider in either position.
# (The A capture has a fourth press, DOWN, after those three.) The shades are
# set to channel A.

